T_HEART = "Trace one loop: body, right atrium, right ventricle, lungs, left atrium, left ventricle, body. Right side handles oxygen-poor blood."
T_PULM = "Arteries leave the heart, veins return to it. The pulmonary pair is the one place where the oxygen labels flip."
T_EKG = "EKG: P = atria depolarize, QRS = ventricles depolarize, T = ventricles repolarize."
T_AP = "Action potential: Na+ rushes in to rise, K+ flows out to fall. Na+ channels then sit inactivated for a moment."
T_NEPH = "Nephron in order: glomerulus filters, proximal tubule reclaims most, loop builds the gradient, distal tubule and collecting duct fine-tune under hormones."
T_HORM = "For any hormone, pin down three things: where it is made, what triggers it, what it does."
T_PIT = "Posterior pituitary only stores and releases ADH and oxytocin, which the hypothalamus makes. Everything else pituitary is anterior."
T_SARC = "When a sarcomere shortens, the filaments slide and do not shrink: A band constant, I band and H zone narrow."
T_DIG = "Match enzyme, source and target: amylase starch, pepsin protein in acid, lipase fat with bile, brush border enzymes finish the job."
T_IG = "Antibody classes: G crosses the placenta, A guards mucosa, M comes first, E allergies, D sits on B cells."
T_MHC = "MHC I is on all nucleated cells and talks to CD8 cells (1 x 8 = 8). MHC II is on antigen-presenting cells and talks to CD4 cells (2 x 4 = 8)."
T_CYCLE = "Menstrual cycle: FSH grows the follicle, estrogen rises, the LH surge releases the egg, the corpus luteum makes progesterone."
T_GAM = "Sperm: continuous from puberty, four per meiosis. Eggs: started before birth, paused twice, one per meiosis."
T_FETAL = "Two fetal shortcuts skip the lungs: foramen ovale (right atrium to left atrium) and ductus arteriosus (pulmonary artery to aorta)."
T_ANS = "Sympathetic: short preganglionic fiber, norepinephrine at the target. Parasympathetic: acetylcholine at both synapses, muscarinic at the target."
T_BONE = "Osteoblasts build bone, osteoclasts break it down, osteocytes maintain it."

